From: ProjectM TV maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Treat parsed file booleans as nonzero integers

Match original MilkDrop2 finite integer file flags and custom-wave enable.
Preserve GetInt parsing, invalid/range defaults, case-insensitive keys and
normalized first occurrence. Negative flags now activate the same path as
positive flags across main settings, custom waves and custom shapes.
Keep unconditional init and one-evaluation Native geometry replay unchanged.
No new equation evaluation is added except authored work formerly disabled
by a negative enable value. Nonfinite/out-of-range strings retain defaults.

Original: vis_milk2/state.cpp:1191,1406 and milkdropfs.cpp:2600.

diff --git a/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/PresetFileParser.cpp b/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/PresetFileParser.cpp
--- a/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/PresetFileParser.cpp
+++ b/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/PresetFileParser.cpp
@@ -142,7 +142,7 @@
-
+
 auto PresetFileParser::GetBool(const std::string& key, bool defaultValue) -> bool
 {
-    return GetInt(key, static_cast<int>(defaultValue)) > 0;
+    return GetInt(key, static_cast<int>(defaultValue)) != 0;
 }
-
+
 auto PresetFileParser::GetString(const std::string& key, const std::string& defaultValue) -> std::string
